{
  "extends": "expo/tsconfig.base",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strict": true,
    "baseUrl": "./",
    "ignoreDeprecations": "5.0",
    "paths": {
      "@assets/*": [
        "./src/assets/*"
      ],
      "@components/*": [
        "./src/components/*"
      ],
      "@routes/*": [
        "./src/routes/*"
      ],
      "@screens/*": [
        "./src/screens/*"
      ],
      "@storage/*": [
        "./src/storage/*"
      ],
      "@theme/*": [
        "./src/theme/*"
      ],
      "@utils/*": [
        "./src/utils/*"
      ],
      "@domain/*": [
        "./src/domain/*"
      ],
      "@services/*": [
        "./src/services/*"
      ],
      "@stores/*": [
        "./src/stores/*"
      ],
      "@hooks/*": [
        "./src/hooks/*"
      ]
    }
  },
  "//": "Saida do `expo export`. O `expo/tsconfig.base` NAO exclui nada, entao sem isto o tsc entra no bundle gerado e morre com 'Maximum call stack size exceeded' — sem citar arquivo e sem pista de que a causa foi ter buildado o site. Aviso do Andre em 27/08, depois de pisar nisso no parceiro.",
  "exclude": ["dist", "web-build", "node_modules", ".expo", "coverage", ".claude"]
}
